    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="0740" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/837a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Odessa</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Ray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-12T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                                1917, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please report immediately conditions your district as affecting army, food
                    supplies, sentiment for separate peace. What information have you regarding
                    progress of reported effort by Alexeev,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d770-f1"/>
                        Kornilov,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d770-f2"/> and Kaledin<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d770-f3"/> to reconstruct loyal portions of army.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d770-f1" n="1" xml:id="d770-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. M. V. Alexeev, from March to June 1917 Commander in Chief of the Russian
                    Army and in September 1917 Chief of Staff; at this time engaged with Kornilov
                    and others in the formation of the Volunteer Army.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d770-f2" n="2" xml:id="d770-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. L. G. Kornilov, in July 1917 commander of the southwestern front and from
                    July to September 1917 Commander in Chief of the Russian Army.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d770-f3" n="3" xml:id="d770-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. A.M. Kaledin, Ataman of the Don Cossacks.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
